    "notes": "Like 39-Across, this crossword is overstuffed. One Down answer in each column is something that might be found in a kitchen, and the answer has one letter too many. Drop that letter to the row beneath the grid [that row is not shown in the electronic version--just make a row of 15 boxes underneath the grid] so that what remains is still a word. When you have finished the puzzle, the source of the problem will become clear."
